    "2": {
      "note": "Bigger numbers in Cantonese are built like Lego: <em>ji6 sap6</em> (二十) is literally \"two-ten\" = 20, <em>saam1 sap6 ng5</em> (三十五) is \"three-ten-five\" = 35. Hundreds use <strong>baak3</strong> (百) and thousands use <strong>cin1</strong> (千). For Hong Kong money, <strong>man1</strong> (蚊) is the colloquial word for dollar (HKD) — you'll hear it everywhere from markets to taxis. <em>gei2 do1</em> (幾多) means \"how many\" or \"how much\" — pair it with <em>cin2</em> (錢, money) to ask prices.",
